WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:01.020
So Hank a couple days ago

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.020
I had a fairly important phone call like

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.660
important enough that I can't tell you

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:09.450
specifically who I was talking to and I was pretty nervous about it because I always get nervous about phone calls.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:14.130
But it was going pretty well, and then when it came time for the phone call to end. They were like: "Alright!

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:17.069
Well take care! Talk to you soon!" And I said: "Best wishes!"

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.680
Best wishes?

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:31.260
You know they hung up the phone and they said: "Did that guy just say goodbye to us by saying 'best wishes?'"

00:00:31.529 --> 00:00:37.439
So just a memo to all the teenage nerdfighters out there who are wondering will my self-consciousness ever go away: Yeah,

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:42.419
no, it won't. Best wishes. Hank, as you'll no doubt notice, puff levels

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.910
have gone down considerably. When I went to the barber

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.800
I said, "Can you just take a little bit off the top?

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.189
I like it to be pretty long and messy." And she said, "Sure thing."

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:53.789
I took off my glasses like I always do when I get a haircut. 20 minutes later

00:00:53.789 --> 00:00:59.579
I put my glasses back on and I was bald. And she said (and I'm quoting her directly here), "Is that short enough?"

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:03.719
No, actually could you make it a little bit shorter because when I said just a little bit off the top

00:01:03.719 --> 00:01:08.849
I like it long and messy what I meant was: I'm joining the marines. So Hank, as you know,

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:10.060
I was gonna try to do a question Tuesday

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:14.189
video today where I attempt to break the world record for "number of questions answered in four minutes."

00:01:14.189 --> 00:01:19.169
But unfortunately it's going to have to wait until next Tuesday because I haven't even finished going through all of the questions.

00:01:19.689 --> 00:01:24.869
Because there were more than 2,000 questions. So question Tuesday will be next Tuesday. In the meantime

00:01:24.869 --> 00:01:30.959
let's do some housekeeping. Housekeeping item number one: if you live in or near Spartanburg, South Carolina, you should come see me

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:36.210
speak about my books and sign them on Friday? Saturday? Saturday! This Saturday

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:41.519
I'll be signing in the morning in the afternoon and speaking at two o'clock at the Spartanburg Public library Jambo Read.

00:01:41.799 --> 00:01:43.259
Jambo Read is a nice pun.

00:01:43.259 --> 00:01:48.989
It's like all the fun of a party but with books. Housekeeping item number two: if you live in or near Depew,

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:53.610
New York - and I know a lot of nerdfighters do - then please attend the meeting on Tuesday, March 4th

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:58.259
when they're going to talk about whether to keep my book "Looking for Alaska" in the curriculum at Depew High School.

00:01:58.259 --> 00:02:02.819
You can find out more in the video info. Housekeeping item number three: the nerdfighter blurbing book club. Hank,

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:07.290
this is off topic, but I really like saying blurbing. Blurbing is one of those words that when you say it,

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:12.539
it sounds like your voice is turning into a robot voice.  [in a robot voice] Blurbing. Blurbing. Blurbing. Blurbing.

00:02:12.819 --> 00:02:17.669
Blurbing. Blurbing. Anyway nerdfighters, if you want to participate in the blurbing and potentially win fantastic prizes

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:21.989
you need to write a blurb about Maureen Johnson's book "13 Little Blue Envelopes" of

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:26.970
10 words or less and post it as a blog post in your profile at the Ning.

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:32.459
We'll read them all, I promise. The deadline is Sunday at midnight. Then we're going to go to bed promptly at 12:01,

00:02:32.459 --> 00:02:38.548
get some sleep, wake up the next morning, and start the next book in the nerdfighter Blurbing book club: "Slaughterhouse-five" by Kurt Vonnegut

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:42.299
which I'm picking because it's really good, and I haven't read it for a long time. Plus

00:02:42.299 --> 00:02:47.939
it's published all over the world so international nerdfighters can participate, too. And finally housekeeping item number four: Hank

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:52.079
it's no secret that I really love two things. The first is nerdfighter babies

00:02:52.079 --> 00:02:54.929
and the second is when a nerdfighter finds another nerdfighter

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:59.190
and they fall in nerdfighter-like. I like nerdfighter-like so much partly because it makes me feel

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:03.929
like, you know if it wasn't for us then there might be less like in the world.

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:08.819
Which is a really good feeling and a nice counterbalance to having people say, "I don't want to listen to this freak.

00:03:08.819 --> 00:03:12.809
I want to see giraffes doing it." Hank, there's been quite a lot of nerdfighter-like going around lately

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:15.119
thanks partly to the Ning which allows, you know,

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:19.079
nerdfighters to meet other nerdfighters and look at their interests and read their blog posts

00:03:19.209 --> 00:03:20.700
and see their pictures and everything.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:25.769
But the particular reason I'm mentioning it is that the vloglovers YouTube channel is back.

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:32.759
Noted secret siblings Abbey Songs From a Hat and Todd Toddly are a nerdfighter-like. Yay!

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:35.819
That's right, Hank. They're touching and

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:38.170
hugging and

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:41.280
nothing else. Hank, speaking of Nuclear chain reactions of awesome,

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:46.410
I hope I see some nerdfighters in Spartanburg, South Carolina on Saturday, and I'll see you later this week

00:03:47.019 --> 00:03:53.879
singing - I'm very excited, but I'm not going to tell them what you're singing about. Hank, I think there's only one thing left to say:

00:03:54.459 --> 00:03:56.459
Best wishes!

